course: dictionary
lesson: 4013
title: Garlic: one word, many places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Garlic is a plant that looks like a small onion. It has a strong smell and taste, and cooks use it to flavour food such as pasta and bread. Its bulb splits into small parts called cloves, so a recipe might ask for «a clove of garlic».
explain: Context tells you which part of garlic the writer means. «Crush garlic» in a recipe means squash it so the flavour comes out. In a science lesson, garlic is a bulb that grows underground, like an onion. In a story, garlic keeps vampires away, but that is only a story idea.
explain: Read the whole sentence to find the clue. «Onions, garlic, leeks and chives damage red blood cells in cats and dogs.» Here garlic is not a tasty treat. The words damage and cats and dogs tell you it can make pets ill.
fact: Garlic is a plant like a small onion, with a strong smell and taste.
fact: Its bulb splits into parts called cloves, so you can say «a clove of garlic».
fact: Garlic is uncountable: we say «some garlic», not «three garlics».
fact: «Garlic» is poisonous for cats and dogs, so pets must never eat it.
exercise: «Crush garlic and fry it in oil for the pasta sauce.» What is garlic in this sentence? | A sweet fruit | *A plant like a small onion, used to flavour food | A type of stone
exercise: Mum says «a clove of garlic» in a recipe. What is a clove? | A garlic-flavoured sweet | A whole garlic plant | *One of the small parts that a garlic bulb splits into
exercise: «Onions, garlic, leeks and chives damage red blood cells in cats and dogs.» What does this tell you about garlic for pets? | It helps cats grow strong | *It is dangerous for cats and dogs | It is a sweet kind of fruit | It is the best food for a dog
test: «The moonrat smells strongly of garlic or onion.» What does the sentence tell you? | It smells sweet, like flowers | *It has a strong smell, like garlic | It has no smell at all | It smells like fruit
test: Why can we not say «three garlics»? | *Garlic is uncountable, so we say «some garlic» | Garlic is always a fruit | Garlic has no plural because it is too small | Garlics are only grown in summer
exam: «Human food is not pet food: onions, garlic, chocolate, grapes, salt and the sweetener xylitol can make dogs and cats very ill.» What must a pet eat, according to this sentence? | Onions and garlic | Anything left on the plate | *Its own food | Human food like grapes
